        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "Interesting situation.\n\nMicrosoft Windows NT 6.1 itself has received support for security updates since 2009 and will continue to do so [until at least January 13, 2026](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Windows_Server_2008_R2#Paid_extended_updates) (along with other approaches such as micropatching and sandboxing). It is [still actively used](https://gs.statcounter.com/windows-version-market-share/desktop/worldwide) by some people.\nThe latest [Skype](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Skype) is still running with it, but is announced to be shut down on May 5, 2025.\n\nWhile the official, lightweight chat client using the Tox protocol for Windows – with user privacy and no advartising in mind – expects users to either stick with older versions or switch to one of the bloated, ad-packed, and patronizing later versions of Windows with different hardware requirements.",
